# Deploy workflow (Atlas Pricing / Vertex)

- **GitHub repo:** `jganny/atlas_pricing_app`
- **Live site:** Firebase Hosting project `vertex-35d95` (https://vertex-35d95.web.app)
- **Auto-deploy is OFF.** The workflow lives at `.github/workflows-disabled/deploy-hosting.yml` (moved out of `.github/workflows/` on 2026-08-30 at the owner's request — pushing to `main` no longer deploys anything). Do not move it back or re-add a workflow that deploys on push without the owner's explicit go-ahead.

## After every release

1. Bump `version.txt`, `APP_VERSION` in `app-v4.js`, and all `?v=` cache-bust strings in `index.html`.
2. Commit with a clear message (e.g. `v129.04: …`) and push to `origin main` on GitHub.
3. Deploy is a separate, explicit step — `firebase deploy --only hosting --project vertex-35d95` — run only when the owner asks for that specific release to go live.
4. Confirm https://vertex-35d95.web.app/version.txt shows the new version afterward.

## Do not

- Change pricing formulas, quote save/load logic, or existing Firestore quote data unless explicitly requested.
- Re-enable auto-deploy-on-push without the owner explicitly asking for it.
- Create pull requests unless the user explicitly asks — push to `main` for this project.

## Branding

- Market brand: **Vertex** (never show Namahsky Nexus in UI).
